9a40ae","cmd-1f1e9dea0d7e4a62","cmd-8341863fc2aa4baa","cmd-6af19aec5e834c1c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Filesystem-level XFS quota enforcement limits datauser to 100M under /srv/data, survives restart, and leaves the original RHEL release and kernel intact. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered system, mount, quota, data, and enforcement were directly observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots cover generic platform health rather than quota-specific state; quota configuration and behavior are established by direct executor command evidence.","The instruction uses “100 MB” while XFS reports the configured limit as “100M” and the tests interpret it as 100 MiB (104,857,600 bytes), a conventional filesystem-tool interpretation."]}
